          "title": "You'll want to know: کثیف",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کثیف (kasif) — \"dirty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حوله های حمام کثیف بود. Hole-hâ-ye hammâm kasif bud. The bathroom towels were dirty."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The opposite of tamiz. Note the letter ث, said s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kasif was borrowed from Arabic kaṯīf (EtymDB). In Arabic the word usually means 'thick, dense'; in Persian the sense moved to 'dirty'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
