            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "آب گرمکن (âbgarmkon) خراب بود و آب حمام سرد بود. Âbgarmkon kharâb bud va âb-e hammâm sard bud. The water heater was broken and the bath water was cold."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "âb 'water' + garm 'hot' + kon 'making'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "âbgarmkon is a native compound: âb 'water' goes back to Middle Persian āb (EtymDB), garm 'warm' is usually traced to Middle Persian garm, and kon is the present stem of kardan 'to do'."
            }
          ]
        },
